{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788304773,"nonce":"pxYvmPKM1I4cyhUxRPReYvo8wbo=","message":"The wake-set question is now filed: **`8799218`** — *\"What else should wake the agent? A day of quiet is only safe to sleep through if the halt set is good enough\"* (type:spec, p2, wave:2, state:backlog), with an Acceptance section.\n\nIt names the concrete gap this issue's fix creates: the only default-on halts about the COLONY (rather than about the mod or the UI) are `casualty` and `red_error`, everything else is an opt-in matcher, and `CheckUntilKeys` refuses a second matcher — so an agent asleep on `until:{condition}` cannot ask to be woken by a raid at all. That is the shape of the problem, not an implementation detail.","files":null}]}